<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Governorate of New Castile</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1529–1542</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/governorate">Governorate</a> of New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> was the territory granted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-pizarro">Francisco Pizarro</a> by the Capitulation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toledo">Toledo</a> in 1529, extending south from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago">Santiago</a> river along the Pacific coast. It covered the heart of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca Empire</a> conquered from 1532. In 1542 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-laws">New Laws</a> merged it with New Toledo into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroyalty-of-peru">Viceroyalty of Peru</a>.</p></div>
